   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response to Migration Situation in Mexico and Central America</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">During this six-month project, IOM aims to respond to the unique and evolving humanitarian needs of Venezuelan migrants, particularly those stranded or in precarious situations in light of the U.S. new migration and border policies pertaining to Venezuelan nationals. IOM&#x2019;s proposed response is based on information collected through IOM&#x2019;s Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) in all three project countries (Costa Rica, Mexico, and Panama) which has determined the urgent priority needs of migrants to be: temporary collective shelters, protection, food assistance, non-food items, health/Mental Health and Psychosocial Services (MHPSS) and access to information regarding processes and available services. To ensure delivery of this key assistance, IOM must support frontline actors in enhancing coordination (not only at a local level but also between countries and at a regional level) and provide capacity building activities for migration officials and Civil Society Organizations (CSOs). In addition, to ensure a cohesive and efficient response and evidence-based interventions, ongoing information management activities are needed.</narrative>
  </description>
